          "title": "You'll want to know: दीपावलिः",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "दीपावलिः — dīpāvaliḥ — \"the festival of lamps; a row of lamps\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "दीपावल्यां सर्वत्र दीपाः ज्वलन्ति। dīpāvalyāṃ sarvatra dīpāḥ jvalanti. At Diwali lamps burn everywhere."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A feminine noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "दीपावलिः (dīpāvaliḥ) is built from dīpa, \"a lamp\", and āvali, \"a row\"; MW gives dīpāvali as a row of lights, a night illumination, and the festival of Diwali is its modern use (MW)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
