              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "दीपयति — dīpayati — \"lights; kindles\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "बालिका गृहस्य द्वारे दीपं दीपयति। bālikā gṛhasya dvāre dīpaṃ dīpayati. The girl lights a lamp at the door of the house."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (she …): सा दीपं दीपितवती, sā dīpaṃ dīpitavatī."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "दीपयति (dīpayati) comes from the root √dīp, \"to blaze, shine\", as in dīpa, \"a lamp\", in its causative form: to set alight, kindle (MW)."
            }
          ]
        },
